e_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible: 4.1.2 RC and up\n- Not reproducible: 4.1.1 stable and lower\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev (e267cbee0) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 580 2048SP (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21921.1000) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the editor window is resized to a certain size, hover a tab in the `TabBar` theme editor can trigger an infinite recursion between `TabBar::_update_cache` and `TabBar::_update_hover` that results in Godot crash. This issue is similar to #100775 but for the issue author the crash started in 4.3 dev 6, maybe due the OS difference.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d241a8a-59eb-4842-abf2-efaf9092aae0\n\n<br>\n\nBisecting shows the commit 3bb05da from pr #81202 (cherry-picked from #78777) as the culprit:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d4b4f48-780e-405d-b3b6-414d6b4a4b2f)\n\nCC @YeldhamDev\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the mrp\n2. Open the `default.tres`\n3. Resize the window width just enough to show the second tab in the theme editor\n4. Hover the second tab in theme editor\n\nIf don't crash, shrink the window width and do steps 3 and 4 again.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18400687/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}